@startuml NotaryProgramLifecycleSeq1

title Notary Program Lifecycle (via Squads Multisig 2-of-4)

autonumber "<b>##"

box "Multisig Key Holders" #LightGray
actor "Key Holder 1" as KH1
actor "Key Holder 2" as KH2
actor "Key Holder 3" as KH3
actor "Key Holder 4" as KH4
actor "Key Holder Successor" as KHS
actor "Temporary Deployer Key\n(ephemeral)" as DEP
end box

box "Solana" #DFF3FF
participant "Squads Program\n(2-of-4 multisig)" as SQ
participant "Notary Program" as NP
database "On-chain State\n(Program + Metadata)" as CHAIN
end box


note over KH1,KH4
Four independent operators hold signer keys.
Threshold for privileged actions is 2-of-4.
end note

== Squads Multisig Registration (PDA Initialization) ==

KH2 -> KH1: <color brown>**DF_SHARE_MEMBER_PUBKEY**</color>\nShare member public key
KH3 -> KH1: <color brown>**DF_SHARE_MEMBER_PUBKEY**</color>\nShare member public key
KH4 -> KH1: <color brown>**DF_SHARE_MEMBER_PUBKEY**</color>\nShare member public key
KH1 -> KH1: <color brown>**DF_VALIDATE_MEMBER_PUBKEYS**</color>\nValidate collected member pubkeys

note right of KH1
Validation should prove key ownership, not only key format.
Recommended control: out-of-band challenge signature per member key,
verified before multisig registration.
end note

KH1 -> SQ: <color brown>**DF_REGISTER_MULTISIG**</color>\nSelect createKey (unique seed/public key)
SQ -> SQ: Derive multisig PDA from (createKey + Squads program ID)

KH1 -> SQ: <color brown>**DF_REGISTER_MULTISIG**</color>\nSubmit initial member pubkeys + threshold
note right of SQ
v4 registration includes role assignment per member key:
- Proposer
- Voter
- Executor
end note

KH1 -> SQ: <color brown>**DF_REGISTER_MULTISIG**</color>\nSign creation tx and pay rent for account storage
SQ -> CHAIN: <color brown>**DF_REGISTER_MULTISIG**</color>\nCreate Multisig account state at derived PDA
SQ -> CHAIN: <color brown>**DF_REGISTER_MULTISIG**</color>\nPersist member pubkeys, threshold, and role config

note over SQ,CHAIN
Multisig account state is the global Squad configuration.
Registered pubkeys become authorized controllers of the Squads vault/governance.
end note

note over KH1,SQ
Creation process summary:
1) Seed selection (createKey) for uniqueness
2) Member input (initial pubkeys; some UI flows cap initial input e.g., up to 5)
3) Deployment transaction (creator signs + funds rent)
4) Registration on-chain (members + threshold + roles)
end note

== Deployment Ceremony (Bootstrap + Handover) ==

note over DEP,SQ
Temporary deployer key exists only for bootstrap.
Ceremony objective: deploy -> transfer authority -> retire key.
end note

note over DEP,SQ #E6F3FF
Countermeasure mapping:
- ATOMIC_AUTHORITY_HANDOVER
- EPHEMERAL_DEPLOY_KEY_RETIREMENT
- SECURE_DEPLOYMENT_ENVIRONMENT
end note

DEP -> NP: Bootstrap deploy using temporary deployment key
NP -> CHAIN: Program deployed (temporarily mutable during bootstrap window)
note right of DEP
SECURE_DEPLOYMENT_ENVIRONMENT:
Use hardened, dedicated deployment environment;
avoid personal developer laptops.
end note

KH1 -> SQ: <color brown>**DF_DEPLOY_NOTARY_PROGRAM**</color>\nPropose deployment transaction
SQ -> SQ: Record proposal (status: pending)

KH2 -> SQ: Vote approve
KH3 -> SQ: Vote approve
SQ -> SQ: Quorum reached (2-of-4)

SQ -> NP: <color brown>**DF_DEPLOY_NOTARY_PROGRAM**</color>\nExecute deploy instruction
NP -> CHAIN: <color brown>**DF_DEPLOY_NOTARY_PROGRAM**</color>\nWrite program code + initial authorities
NP --> SQ: Deployment success

KH1 -> SQ: ATOMIC_AUTHORITY_HANDOVER\nPropose authority transfer (temporary key -> Squads PDA)
KH2 -> SQ: Vote approve
SQ -> NP: Execute authority transfer
NP -> CHAIN: Upgrade authority = Squads multisig PDA

DEP -> DEP: EPHEMERAL_DEPLOY_KEY_RETIREMENT\nRetire temporary deployment key

note over DEP,CHAIN #FFCCCC
If temporary key is not retired immediately,
exfiltration risk persists beyond ceremony.
end note

== Post-Deployment Verification ==

note over KH1,CHAIN #E6F3FF
PRE_USE_ONCHAIN_VERIFICATION:
Mandatory on-chain verification before first use.
end note

KH1 -> CHAIN: <color brown>**DF_VERIFY_DEPLOYMENT**</color>\nRead deployed program ID / code hash / authority state
KH2 -> CHAIN: <color brown>**DF_VERIFY_DEPLOYMENT**</color>\nIndependently confirm expected release artifact

KH1 -> CHAIN: Confirm no unexpected privileged tx during bootstrap window

alt Verification passed
	KH1 -> SQ: Record governance note (deployment valid)
else Verification failed
	KH1 -> SQ: Raise incident and pause privileged operations
end

== Runtime Administration ==

KH1 -> SQ: <color brown>**DF_CREATE_NETWORK**</color>\nPropose admin action (add Corda network)
KH4 -> SQ: Vote approve
SQ -> NP: <color brown>**DF_CREATE_NETWORK**</color>\nExecute create_network admin instruction
NP -> CHAIN: <color brown>**DF_CREATE_NETWORK**</color>\nPersist new Corda network configuration

KH2 -> SQ: <color brown>**DF_NOTARY_ADMIN**</color>\nPropose admin action (authorize/revoke notary)
KH3 -> SQ: Vote approve
SQ -> NP: <color brown>**DF_NOTARY_ADMIN**</color>\nExecute admin instruction
NP -> CHAIN: <color brown>**DF_NOTARY_ADMIN**</color>\nPersist admin state changes

== Program Upgrade Lifecycle ==

KH2 -> SQ: <color brown>**DF_UPGRADE_NOTARY_PROGRAM**</color>\nPropose notary program upgrade
KH3 -> SQ: Vote approve
SQ -> SQ: Quorum reached (2-of-4)
SQ -> NP: <color brown>**DF_UPGRADE_NOTARY_PROGRAM**</color>\nExecute upgrade transaction
NP -> CHAIN: <color brown>**DF_UPGRADE_NOTARY_PROGRAM**</color>\nStore upgraded program code

KH1 -> CHAIN: Re-check code hash and authority constraints
KH2 -> CHAIN: Confirm upgrade matches approved artifact

== Transition to Immutability ==

KH1 -> SQ: <color brown>**DF_IMMUTABLE_LOCK**</color>\nPropose lock/immutable finalization
KH2 -> SQ: Vote approve
SQ -> NP: <color brown>**DF_IMMUTABLE_LOCK**</color>\nExecute immutable lock (disable upgrades)
NP -> CHAIN: <color brown>**DF_IMMUTABLE_LOCK**</color>\nMark program immutable

note over NP,CHAIN
After immutable lock, no further code upgrades are possible.
Governance can still operate only through allowed runtime admin paths.
end note

== Attempted Upgrade After Lock ==

KH3 -> SQ: Propose program upgrade (post-lock)
KH4 -> SQ: Vote approve
SQ -> NP: Execute upgrade attempt
NP --> SQ: Reject (program immutable)

== Membership Changes After Creation ==

KH2 -> SQ: <color brown>**DF_MEMBER_UPDATE**</color>\nPropose member update (add/remove key)
KH3 -> SQ: Vote approve
KH4 -> SQ: Vote approve
SQ -> SQ: Quorum reached under current membership policy
SQ -> CHAIN: <color brown>**DF_MEMBER_UPDATE**</color>\nUpdate multisig member list and role assignments

== Key Holder Succession (Anti-Bricking Control) ==

KHS -> KH1: <color brown>**DF_KEY_HOLDER_SUCCESSION**</color>\nShare successor wallet pubkey + ownership proof
KH1 -> SQ: <color brown>**DF_KEY_HOLDER_SUCCESSION**</color>\nPropose succession member update (add successor)
KH2 -> SQ: Vote approve
KH3 -> SQ: Vote approve
SQ -> CHAIN: <color brown>**DF_KEY_HOLDER_SUCCESSION**</color>\nRegister successor as active multisig member

KH1 -> SQ: <color brown>**DF_KEY_HOLDER_SUCCESSION**</color>\nPropose retirement/removal of departing key holder
KH2 -> SQ: Vote approve
KH4 -> SQ: Vote approve
SQ -> CHAIN: <color brown>**DF_KEY_HOLDER_SUCCESSION**</color>\nFinalize member rotation (remove old key)

note over KHS,SQ
Successor onboarding and rotation must happen through Squads governance transactions.
No direct off-chain replacement of member keys is possible.
end note

note over KH1,CHAIN
Member list changes are only possible through the multisig itself.
No external actor can directly rewrite registered pubkeys.
end note

@enduml
